{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"I submitted the mitigation, but I could not find the cause of the degradation, so the fix is unconfirmed.\n\n**What I checked**\n- All application pods are Running and Ready, and every Service has healthy endpoints.\n- Frontend requests to hotels, recommendations, user, and reservation all returned HTTP 200 in about 1–7 ms. A 300-request load test at concurrency 30 also ran cleanly.\n- Application logs show no errors beyond startup-time Consul connection refusals. Nodes report no memory, disk, or PID pressure.\n\n**What I changed**\n- Suspended the `audit-log-archiver` CronJob in `hotel-reservation`. Its `fluent-bit-sidecar` never exits, so each minute's Job stays active and new pods pile up. It is the only anomaly I found, but it is not on the user request path, so I don't think it explains the degradation.\n\n**Open items**\n- Three archiver pods are still present and NotReady. I left them in place. Deleting them would remove audit records.\n- The CronJob is suspended, not fixed. Someone needs to decide whether it is needed and how its sidecar should exit, and whether to re-enable it.\n- Jaeger returned no traces for the frontend, so I could not check trace-level latency."}}
